gredient-nut-fruit"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nut_(fruit)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Afghan cuisine","cuisine/afghan-cuisine",[["Kabuli pulao","dish/kabuli-pulao"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Carrots","ingredient/carrots"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Raisin","ingredient/raisin"],["Raisins","ingredient/raisins"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Steamed rice","ingredient/steamed-rice"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a9/Caov2_002_phd.jpg/500px-Caov2_002_phd.jpg","w":500,"h":323,"by":"USDA-NRCS PLANTS Database","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caov2_002_phd.jpg"}},"dish/qatlama":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/qatlama","n":"Qatlama","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 3 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Qatlama, qattama, katlama, kattama, (Kazakh: қаттама, romanized: qattama; Kyrgyz: каттама, both pronounced [qɑttɑmɑ]), katmer (Turkish: katmer), katma (Bulgarian: катма), qator, gambir (Mongolian: гамбир, pronounced [ɢæmʲbʲĭɾ]) is a fried layered bread common in the cuisines of Central Asia, Pakistan and Turkey."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-qatlama"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qatlama"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Kazakh cuisine","cuisine/kazakh-cuisine"],["Kyrgyz cuisine","cuisine/kyrgyz-cuisine"],["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Onion","ingredient/onion"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Ozlem's Turkish Table","ref":"site/ozlemsturkishtable-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"ozlemsturkishtable.com","note":"Turkish-born cook and teacher Ozlem Warren's blog of home-style Turkish recipes.","url":"https://ozlemsturkishtable.com/tag/turkish-recipes/page/9","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Kazakh cuisine","links":[["Beshbarmak","dish/beshbarmak"],["Boortsog","dish/boortsog"],["Chorba","dish/chorba"],["Dimlama","dish/dimlama"],["Kuurdak","dish/kuurdak"],["Naryn (dish)","dish/naryn-dish"],["Orama (dish)","dish/orama-dish"],["Peremech","dish/peremech"],["Pilaf","dish/pilaf"],["Qazı","dish/qaz"],["Shakarap","dish/shakarap"],["Shalgam","dish/shalgam"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/24/Turkish_katmer.jpg/500px-Turkish_katmer.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"E4024","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Turkish_katmer.jpg"}},"ingredient/fresh-cheese":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/fresh-cheese","n":"Fresh cheese","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["There are different types of cheese, which can be grouped or classified according to criteria such as: length of fermentation, texture, production method, fat content, animal source of the milk, and or region of origin. These may be used either singly or in combination, with no method used universally. The most common traditional is based on moisture content, which is then further down by content and curing or ripening methods."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-fresh-cheese"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fresh_cheese"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["German cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine",[["Spundekäs","dish/spundekas"]]],["Thuringian cuisine","cuisine/german-cuisine-thuringia",[["Spundekäs","dish/spundekas"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Quark","ingredient/quark"]]}]},"ingredient/rhizopus":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/rhizopus","n":"Rhizopus","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Rhizopus is a genus of common saprophytic fungi on plants and  specialized parasites on animals. They are found in a wide variety of organic substances, including \"mature fruits and vegetables\", jellies, syrups, leather, bread, peanuts, and tobacco. They are multicellular. Some Rhizopus species are opportunistic human pathogens that often cause fatal disease called mucormycosis. This widespread genus includes at least eight species."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-rhizopus"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhizopus"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Tempeh","dish/tempeh"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Acetic acid","ingredient/acetic-acid"],["Rhizopus oligosporus","ingredient/rhizopus-oligosporus"],["Soybean","ingredient/soybean"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/9a/Structure_of_Rhizopus_spp.-english.JPG/500px-Structure_of_Rhizopus_spp.-english.JPG","w":500,"h":406,"by":"Unknown author","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Structure_of_Rhizopus_spp.-english.JPG"}},"dish/frybread":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/frybread","n":"Frybread","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 4 cuisines","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Frybread comes out of hunger. When the U.S. government forced the ",["Diné","cuisine/dine-foodways"]," on the Long Walk to land that couldn't support their crops, and pushed other nations off their homelands, it handed out rations of white flour, lard, sugar and salt. Fried dough from those rations kept families alive."],["Today it's a powwow staple and the base of Indian tacos, and it holds both pride and pain: a sign of survival, and a reminder of the foods that were lost. It's also high in fat and calories. Some critics tie it to diabetes on reservations, while others say the deeper problem is access to healthy food, and many communities are bringing traditional foods back alongside it."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Smithsonian Magazine, Frybread","url":"https://www.smithsonianmag.com/arts-culture/frybread-79191/"},{"name":"Washington State Health Care Authority, Food and survival","url":"https://connections.hca.wa.gov/hca/2025/november/food-and-survival-why-fry-bread-is-not-a-novelty-food"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-frybread"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frybread"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Diné foodways","cuisine/dine-foodways"],["Lakota foodways","cuisine/lakota-foodways"],["Cherokee foodways","cuisine/cherokee-foodways"],["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Lard","ingredient/lard"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Owamni","ref":"site/owamni-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"owamni.com","note":"Sean Sherman's Minneapolis restaurant, cooking only with Indigenous ingredients.","url":"https://owamni.com/","suggested":true},{"name":"Cherokee Tribal Food Distribution Program","ref":"site/food-ebci-nsn-gov","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"food.ebci-nsn.gov","note":"Traditional recipes from the Eastern Band of Cherokee Indians, like Three Sisters stew and chestnut bread.","url":"https://food.ebci-nsn.gov/?p=4673","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Diné foodways","links":[["Blue corn mush","dish/blue-corn-mush"],["Kneel down bread","dish/kneel-down-bread"]]},{"h":"Mentioned in","links":[["Wojapi","dish/wojapi"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/8c/Frybread.jpg/500px-Frybread.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Unknown author","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frybread.jpg"}},"cookbook/british-regional-food":{"t":"book","r":"cookbook/british-regional-food","n":"British Regional Food","c":"#f0b340","crumb":[["Cookbooks","cookbooks"]],"sub":"Cookbook by Mark Hix, 2006","square":true,"suggested":true,"isbn":"9781844002344","intro":[["London chef Mark Hix's survey of regional dishes and producers across Britain."]],"actions":[{"kind":"out","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9781844002344","label":"Open Library"}],"sections":[{"h":"Cuisines it covers","count":1,"links":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine"]]}]}}